course: dictionary
lesson: 11103
title: Whey and curds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from the kitchen, and their meaning is easy to see once you know how food is made. Whey is the watery liquid left over when milk is made into cheese or yoghurt. «Cheese-makers add bacteria and rennet to milk, which separates into solid curds and watery whey.»
explain: Look at the clue words around whey: separates, solid, watery, left over. The solid lumps are the curds, so whey must be the thin liquid that is left behind. Whey is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some whey, not two wheys.
explain: Whey is also in a famous nursery rhyme: «Little Miss Muffet sat on a tuffet, eating her curds and whey.» Curds are the lumps and whey is the watery part. Swap in your meaning to check: lumps and watery liquid still make sense in the rhyme, so you have it right.
fact: Whey is the watery liquid left when milk is made into cheese or yoghurt.
fact: Curds are the solid lumps that form from milk, and they become cheese.
fact: Whey protein is a powder made from whey, and some athletes add it to drinks.
fact: Rennet is a helper that makes milk set into curds, and cheese-makers use it with bacteria.
fact: About ten litres of milk make one kilogram of hard cheese, and most of the milk sugar drains away with the whey.
exercise: «Cheese-makers add bacteria and rennet to milk, which separates into solid curds and watery whey.» What is whey? | A sweet fizzy drink | *The watery liquid left over when milk becomes cheese or yoghurt | The solid lumps used to make cheese | A kind of bread
exercise: In «Little Miss Muffet sat on a tuffet, eating her curds and whey», which word means the solid lumps? | Eating | *Curds | Tuffet | Muffet
exercise: Mia says whey is a kind of cheese. Is she right? | Yes, whey is a hard yellow cheese | Not sure, because whey has no meaning | *No, whey is the watery liquid left over when cheese is made | Yes, because whey is made from curds
test: «Ten litres of milk make about one kilogram of hard cheese, and most of the milk sugar drains away with the whey.» What drains away with the whey? | The solid curds | The rennet | *Most of the milk sugar | The cheese
test: Whey protein is sometimes added to drinks. Where does whey protein come from? | *A powder made from whey | A fizzy drink from yoghurt | A bread made from rennet | A sweet made from curds
exam: Which statement about whey is true? | Whey is a hard yellow cheese | Whey is the solid part, and curds are the watery part | Whey is a kind of bread | *Whey is the watery liquid left over when milk is made into cheese or yoghurt
